OBSOLETE -- disabled 2026-08-06, kept for provenance.

This changed D.InstalledDir to D.Dir inside GccIinstallPrefix handling.  That
code is not clang's: it comes from BUILDROOT's own patch,
package/llvm-project/clang/0001-lib-Driver-ToolChains-Gnu-Use-GCC_INSTALL_PREFIX-in-.patch,
which this tree's buildroot NO LONGER SHIPS -- package/llvm-project/clang/ now
holds only clang.hash, clang.mk and Config.in.  (batocera's older buildroot still
carries it, which is where this came from.)

So GccIinstallPrefix never appears in the source, and the hunk cannot apply:
after retargeting the path for the monorepo layout it still fails with
"Hunk #1 FAILED at 2303".  There is nothing left to fix up.


diff --git a/clang/lib/Driver/ToolChains/Gnu.cpp b/clang/lib/Driver/ToolChains/Gnu.cpp
index e4b922b911..3660a9bda2 100644
--- a/clang/lib/Driver/ToolChains/Gnu.cpp
+++ b/clang/lib/Driver/ToolChains/Gnu.cpp
@@ -2303,7 +2303,7 @@ void Generic_GCC::GCCInstallationDetector::init(
         if (llvm::sys::path::is_relative(GccIinstallPrefix))
         {
             // Use a relative path to gcc from clang install path.
-            Prefixes.push_back(D.InstalledDir + "/" + GccIinstallPrefix.str());
+            Prefixes.push_back(D.Dir + "/" + GccIinstallPrefix.str());
         }
         else
         {
